error[E0277]: this subscriber has no pages to cap
  --> tests/ui/subscriber_batch_slots_without_pages.rs:20:26
   |
20 |     let _capped = handle.batch(nonzero!(64));
   |                          ^^^^^ `batch(..)` caps the pages a page body is handed
   |
help: the trait `ruststream::runtime::CapsPages` is not implemented for `handle`
  --> tests/ui/subscriber_batch_slots_without_pages.rs:13:1
   |
13 | #[subscriber("orders")]
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = note: the cap applies to a page body (`&[T]`, `&[F<'_>]`, `&[Message<H, P>]`), with or without a reply and `Out` slots; a single-message body has no page. To batch single deliveries on the client instead, name the framework's buffer with `buffered(max, wait)`
   = help: the following other types implement trait `ruststream::runtime::CapsPages`:
             HandleValue<Page<T>, R, O, C, H, Doc>
             HandleValue<PageDeserialized<F>, R, O, C, H, Doc>
             HandleValue<PagePair<Hd, P>, R, O, C, H, Doc>
             ReplyValue<V, Dest, Attach>
             Sealed<V>
   = note: required for `SubscriberBuilder<handle, Name, (Open, Open, Open, Open)>` to implement `BatchStep`
   = note: this error originates in the attribute macro `subscriber` (in Nightly builds, run with -Z macro-backtrace for more info)
